# ============================================================
# Mosquitto ACL — Temp-sensors Cloud (base)
# ============================================================
#
# Mounted as /mosquitto/config/acl.base. entrypoint.sh appends one entry per
# registered hub and writes the result to /mosquitto/config/acl, which is the
# file mosquitto reads:
#
#   user 58E6C51540F4
#   topic readwrite sensors/58:E6:C5:15:40:F4/#
#
# Each hub logs in with its own account -- its MAC without colons, password
# devices.api_key -- and can read and write only its own subtree. They all
# used to share one account with readwrite on sensors/#, so whoever held that
# password could read every site and command every hub.
#
# The username cannot be the MAC as written in the topic: mosquitto's password
# file is "user:hash", split at the first colon. That is also why each hub gets
# an explicit entry instead of a "pattern ... %u" line.
# ============================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------
# Backend service account — full access to all topics.
# This user is used by the Node.js backend to subscribe to all
# sensor data and publish pairing responses/commands.
# ----------------------------------------------------------
user backend
topic readwrite #
